THE UNIT
The Procurement and Contract Unit, designation subject to approval of forthcoming organisational structure) provides the Agency’s central expertise for procurement, contracts, grants and prizes, as well as for the upstream basic acts, including ad hoc projects and programmes and contribution agreements. It ensures the sound, consistent and compliant implementation of the Agency’s activities in three main domains:

- General budget procurement: procurement actions financed under the Agency’s general budget, including corporate services, horizontal requirements, administrative needs and operational studies.
- Collaborative procurement: procurement under ad hoc project and programme arrangements, including multi-participant procedures, framework contracts and purchase orders as well as activities funded by EU programmes, such as EDIP.
- Innovation procurement and grants: supports activities linked to innovation, research and technology, including ad hoc R&T contracts, prizes and grants, as well as activities funded by EU programmes, such as EDF.

Main interfaces of the Unit: internal CSD and operational Project Officers acting as budget and business owners; Project Officers within the Collaborative Procurement Centre and the EDA Innovation Centre; ordering Member States and Member States participating in ad hoc R&T projects and programmes; tenderers, applicants, contractors and beneficiaries; the European Commission and its executive agencies; and the EDA Finance and Legal Units.

The Unit works closely with Project Officers and the two operational Centres, from the early definition of requirements and the establishment of the relevant basic acts through to contract or grant implementation. This operating model ensures proximity to operational needs while maintaining central oversight, procedural consistency and appropriate segregation of duties within CSD.

